  "_baseline_note": "Three shipped-604 expectations were pre-registered as guided and observed as model-path. Shipped 604 shortcuts a check-in only when the text STARTS with a question prefix: a leading \"¿\" defeats it (F04), and the other two phrasings never start with one. Corrected to the observed outcome after checking the shipped helper; the candidate expectations were not changed.",
  "_review_cases_note": "Added after the independent review of b2a6ba8 (S2R-1, S2R-2, S2R-11), written before the runs. Both bundles are expected to behave identically on every 'review:' case except the last: a check-in question shipped answered through its substring rule but that is not an accepted whole-request form takes the model path on the candidate. That is the deliberate cost of the F05 fix. The pre-existing 604 records-select case is expected to stay guided on both: it is recorded for the clinician gate, not changed by keyword."
